1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:13,322
Two windows in the same room can differ by a factor of five in how much street pollution they let in. Nobody can tell which is which. SASH measures it, from three Ring devices, without ever looking at an image.

2
00:00:13,322 --> 00:00:20,845
This is a real decision, for a flat with three openings. Open the courtyard window, at this time, for this long.

3
00:00:20,845 --> 00:00:28,165
The street window this household usually reaches for would admit about half as much again, for the same amount of air.

4
00:00:28,165 --> 00:00:36,050
And SASH says how sure it is. Both plans share the same draws, so what is left is the difference between the two windows.

5
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:42,021
SASH never changes how much air the home gets. Only when, and through which window.

6
00:00:42,021 --> 00:00:53,481
Carbon monoxide has no street in it. Between cooking events it decays like a tracer gas, and how fast it decays with each window open gives that window's air exchange rate.

7
00:00:53,481 --> 00:01:03,903
Tracer gas decay normally needs a technician and a cylinder of gas. This household makes the tracer twice a day by cooking, and Ring already measures it.

8
00:01:03,903 --> 00:01:17,415
And SASH refuses to overclaim. Shuffle which window each airing went through, and the courtyard window still wins. The balcony door does not, so SASH says these two are not yet distinguishable.

9
00:01:17,415 --> 00:01:28,871
Now watch the events arrive. Signed webhooks through the shipping receiver, and readings through the same client that reads a Ring account.

10
00:01:28,871 --> 00:01:36,925
A recommendation nobody writes down cannot be wrong later. So SASH publishes the plan and its forecast before the airing happens.

11
00:01:36,925 --> 00:01:46,551
The household opens it, and the flat is simulated again with that window open.

12
00:01:46,551 --> 00:01:56,335
Then the plan is scored against the readings that followed. SASH answers only for airings it proposed and that actually happened.

13
00:01:56,335 --> 00:02:03,481
Harder still: fitted on the first part of the record, SASH prices every airing in the last part before seeing its cost.

14
00:02:03,481 --> 00:02:18,301
Across twenty-four simulated households it had never seen, SASH beat their own habit on sixty-nine of eighty-eight airings, with a median saving of forty-six per cent. On forty homes with identical windows, it claimed a difference on two.

15
00:02:18,301 --> 00:02:32,645
Street air is not always the point. Nine days after linking, this household has just cooked. When the reason to open a window is inside the flat, SASH stops optimising for the street, and only picks the window.

16
00:02:32,645 --> 00:02:38,445
It picks one it has not measured yet, because the fumes fading through it are the measurement.

17
00:02:38,445 --> 00:02:47,423
Each window shows its progress. Guided like this, simulated homes had every window measured in a median of eleven days, instead of forty.

18
00:02:47,423 --> 00:02:51,923
All of it from a camera it never looks through.
